  "scope": [
    "Original GSON/version.asInt marker owner returns exact LOGIN_UI_V2 admission; only that code selects distinct same-View V2 API, never a Swift marker approximation or legacy RowUi fallback.",
    "Same original Rhino/source environment executes actual loginUi(state) and loginAction(action,state,form) with source as java and null standalone book/chapter; original complete row/command validation precedes checked explicit login save.",
    "Returned login object is checked through existing LoginManager raw owner before close/state receipt; known rejection/IO/cancel preserves MayCommit/Committed facts and cannot close. Close-only commands are valid.",
    "BookSourceFormLoginView owns transient V2 session/state/edit/error/countdown, no legacy toolbar OK or non-OK credential persistence; real fields/text/password/label/select/toggle/button use existing native grid controls.",
    "Render input precedence is rendered value then retained session edit then stored; hidden session inputs survive rows changing, current action form contains only current visible fields/toggles. Null select adapter entries are preserved through DTO until raw membership/fallback resolves actual empty EditText values.",
    "Successful render rebases current edits after source response and commits candidate state only after valid projection; failed render preserves old form/state/session and field errors; single task/render and action-specific countdown prevent overlapping dispatch.",
    "Original close/source-change lifecycle cancels/drains existing tasks and close owner before reentry; rapid multiple replacements retain the previous real drain, stale generations cannot publish or clear new handles. No new store, VM, HTTP owner, JS runtime or credential retry cache."
  ],
  "rootNativeRepair": [
    "Preserve the sole existing process runtime and Host; bind/revoke fresh synthetic .invalid source grants.",
    "Record accepted irreversible commit before revision notification; rejection/IO and current owners remain unchanged.",
    "Use actual accepted-write notifications and a bounded test-only lock box to synchronously cancel the existing pending task, including notification-before-registration.",
    "Retain real checked Keychain/reopen/source isolation and committed-cancellation assertions; no second interpreter/router or production test hook."
  ],
